ctional technique so I translate  I take you know I use my own native  tongue to figure out the structure of  the of the language the foreign language  that I'm learning and I use a vibe it's  called a bi-directional technique now I  cannot delve into the details of how  this works but I can assure you that it  works quite well if you know how to do  it because it's also important to know  how to do things so first of all I use  by I use a language series which you  know it's it's very important to stress  the fact that the both day issues does  matter but what matters the most is how  to use language learning material so I  use it in a certain way in order to  absorb the information in that book can  I do this I apply a carry out this  bilingual translation and then I move on  to other things and how do you think  what are the three most important things  in learning language as I said before  attitude is very important attitude  means that the way you you approach  anything in life it is not just about  language learning a positive attitude is  extremely important for example once you  learn the basics of a language once you  can say certain things you can try just  try and use them without a problem  if you meet if you stumble upon a native  speaker you might try to speak to them  in their language even if you know a  little bit of the language itself and  you you can try to apply it in real life  because people tend to use books a lot  but I think that human interaction is  key in language learning is what really  makes a difference so attitude is very  important attitude towards learning in  general and then add it to towards  people because people are the vectors of  a language a language is is alive  because of people because of the people  who speak it and then obviously time a  lot of people complain about the fact  that now they  it's impossible to learn the language  because you don't have a time you have a  family you have other things that you  have to 